# Planted bugs in the rewrite pairs. Each one must make the named check
# miss its declared expectation.
run fv-sqlequiv rewrites.sql
properties DistinctEqualsGroupBy NotInEqualsNotExists
file rewrites.sql

mutation the group-by rewrite drops the group, so duplicates are no longer collapsed
detects DistinctEqualsGroupBy
- SELECT x FROM t GROUP BY x;
+ SELECT x FROM t;

mutation the not-in query is accidentally rewritten to the same query_b, hiding the witness
detects NotInEqualsNotExists
- SELECT * FROM t1 WHERE x NOT IN (SELECT y FROM t2);
+ SELECT * FROM t1 WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM t2 WHERE t2.y = t1.x);

harmless a check comment is reworded
- -- Equivalent rewrite: DISTINCT and a GROUP BY on the same column collapse
+ -- Equivalent rewrite: a GROUP BY on the same column SQLite's DISTINCT uses.
